Z||000019||theogre||08-21-99||03:18 PM||||As I said above..... One of the main advantages to oiled foam, which now have flame retardent oil, and K&N, is the fact they are REUSABLE.<p>Price out good paper, and then when you figure you have to replace it every 6-12 months, the 30-40$us one of these cost is sudenly quite cheap. A recharge kit is good for many charges if you do it right.<p>As for backfires, it's a bit more likely that a 4 cyl could barf on it's filter than the V6. By the time a V6 backfire surge reaches the can, it's had to expend most if not all its heat.
