Z||000022||Pretender||08-22-99||01:49 AM||||I really don't care who this "herb adams" is and if he would of dynoed this mod he would of came to the comclusion that it adds more air flow, and POWER!. Was his car in a wind tunnel when and if it was dynoed anyways?, simply placing a fan in front of the air intake would not be any help!, i doub't that the fan could add 70mph winds into the grill!...i have my opinion and you have yours, grab yourself a $2.50 airfilter from K-Mart and lets line them up!., and bring your friend oh high and mighty HERBI!, he seems to know it all, I bet he also doesn't believe in underdrive pullies/chips/cam gears/ing./plugs and wires either. If i would have my own web page and stated facts would you believe them too?...i'm not dissing you!, so i don't want a hate post but think about it!...call K&N and research your own results, not listening to any old fool who have their own pages...And i'm not dissing any of you guys with pages either!..<p>the results on my box,<br>              flow tests(CFM)<p>new foam filter(Amsoil LT-31)    376 cfm!<p>Paper-(AC A348c, Fram CA326, Hastings AC-145, K-Mart KA-12, Motorcraft FA-71r)   <br>                                 508 cfm!<p>K&N filtercharger         (clean)887 cfm!<br>             (40,000 miles dirty)463 cfm!<p>that shows k&n flows more air then your typical air filter! call them up if you have any questions!<p>
